### Checking the configured mapsFolderName is tsmaps

When the repo was initialised as a Docs Assembler repo in VS Code, the extension writes a configuration file named **`docs-assembler-config.json`** to the **project root**. This file records, among other things, the name of the folder where your maps live. The default value is `tsmaps`.

1. In the VS Code Explorer panel, open **`docs-assembler-config.json`** in the project root.

> In the image below, `docs-assembler-config.json` is at the same level as the `tsmaps/` folder. *- red rectangle*

2. Find the **`repoConfig`** section. *- red rectangle* 

3. Then look for **`mapsFolderName`**. *- green rectangle*


```json
{
    "organisation": "netoftrees",
    "contact": "team@netoftrees.com",
    "gitConfig": {
        "owner": "netoftrees",
        "repo": "docs-assembler-help",
        "branch": "main",
        "publishUrl": "https://netoftrees.com/docs-assembler-help/"
    },
    "repoConfig": {
        "assetFolderName": "δ steps",
        "variableFolderName": "Ω variables",
        "publishFolderName": "pub",
        "docsFolderName": "docs",
        "mapsFolderName": "tsmaps"
    },
    "devConfig": {
        "forceJsDelivr": false
    }
}
```

4. If the value is something **other than `tsmaps`** (for example, `"maps"`), then the default spell-checker filters will not match your maps folder. You must edit the filters in `.cspell.json` to use that value instead.

> For example, if `mapsFolderName` is `"maps"`, change the pattern in `.cspell.json` from `"tsmaps/**/*.tsstp"` to `"maps/**/*.tsstp"`.

